  "calendar": "IL",
  "about": "Bank of Israel Zahav RTGS non-business days (Tel Aviv banks). Zahav runs Sunday-Friday; Fridays and holiday eves are short business days (close 14:00, 14:15 in 2024-25), so Friday closures are listed. Non-business days per Banking Supervision circular H-06-2170 (24 Aug 2005): both days of Rosh Hashanah, Yom Kippur eve, Yom Kippur, Sukkot I, Shemini Atzeret/Simchat Torah, Purim (Tel Aviv, 14 Adar), Pesach I and VII, Independence Day (as moved by law: Fri/Sat -> Thu, Mon -> Tue), Shavuot, Tisha B'Av (Sat -> Sun), plus rest days (Knesset elections; municipal elections from 2018). Gregorian dates computed from the Hebrew calendar and checked against BoI Zahav lists for 2024, 2025, 2026 and 2027 (exact match for weekday closures). Coverage 2005-2027 (BoI has published 2027). The BoI representative rate is additionally not published on Pesach, Rosh Hashanah and Yom Kippur eves, Purim (Jerusalem) and 'holidays abroad' (US holidays): that is a fixing calendar, not a settlement one.",
